  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nAn open 2D Contour now accepts a start pick that exactly equals its natural centerline endpoint.\nClimb uses the first stored point; conventional travel uses the last.\nThe pick does not shift, trim or reverse the run. Every automatic move stays the same.\n\nThe app path supports one selected open DXF sketch chain with Side Auto and no side override.\nIts source is the cutter centerline, which proves the endpoint identity.\nThe existing climb XOR per-chain reverse setting determines the start.\nThe existing WCS mapping rotates the pick with its geometry.\n\nNamed refusals remain for interior, opposite-end and nearby picks; unproved part and stock source mapping;\noffset or extended open boundaries; multiple selected sketch chains when an open chain is present;\nopen-chain exit picks; and the existing tilted-contour cases.\nThe part source refusal also covers its no-material fallback.\nThis is the natural-centerline part of item 5. The remaining source and tilted mapping work stays open under #1473.\n\nDecision: [1473-open-chain-end-picks.md](https://github.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/blob/26872c796815c2babd330a01ff19a82a494cf04b/docs/decisions/1473-open-chain-end-picks.md).\nThe issue adds nine tests and extends the existing short-terminal-leg test without weakening its geometry assertions.\nThe app tests join existing binaries through child modules. No new test binary is added.\n\n## Reproduction before the fix\n\nCanonical baseline: `6898b02ea3195e9124e6113afd6ab3cee38d0c50`.\nInput: centerline `[(0, 0), (20, 0)]`, Lead None, climb enabled, start pick `(0, 0)`;\ntop 10, bottom 0 and stepdown 5.\nExpected: accept that natural endpoint and preserve every automatic move.\n\n```text\ncargo test -j 2 -p camcraft-motion --lib machining2d::contour_run_side::tests::an_open_chain_accepts_a_start_pick_at_its_natural_end -- --exact\n```\n\nThe independent baseline build succeeded. The test exited 101: zero passed, one failed, 790 filtered out.\nIt failed at `contour_run_side_tests.rs:67:52` with:\n\n```text\nnatural end is a valid start: Invalid(\"start point (0.000, 0.000): an open chain starts at its end - a picked start is taken only on closed contours yet; clear the start point\")\n```\n\nThe loop stopped before its conventional case. The fixed pin retains that assertion and exercises both directions.\nThe exact 14-line test-only baseline patch is archived with the phase 6 evidence.\n\n## Verification on the refreshed head\n\nHead: `26872c796815c2babd330a01ff19a82a494cf04b`.\nTree: `083e40a3b2e5985fd46b55bde59e700cee6512f7`.\nBase: `2394b5ad1efc573b7b99a898a02cc4225b4d9893`.\nA separate verifier ran all results below on this exact committed tree.\n\nEnvironment: Windows x64, Rust/Cargo 1.100.1, MSVC, two jobs;\n`CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=2`, worktree-local target and no `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n\nPASS — all ten exact pin commands, selected with `-- --exact`; each ran one test with zero failures or ignores:\n\n`camcraft-motion --lib`:\n\n- `machining2d::contour_run_side::tests::an_open_chain_accepts_a_start_pick_at_its_natural_end`\n- `machining2d::contour_run_side::tests::a_natural_end_pick_keeps_the_lead_on_every_level`\n- `machining2d::contour_run_side::tests::an_open_chain_refuses_starts_other_than_its_exact_natural_end`\n- `machining2d::contour_run_side::tests::an_offset_part_run_refuses_unproved_source_start_picks`\n- `machining2d::contour_run_side::tests::an_open_run_with_a_short_leg_at_an_inside_corner_stops_clear`\n- `machining2d::contour_run_stock::tests::an_offset_stock_run_refuses_unproved_source_start_picks`\n\n`camcraft-app --test area_open`:\n\n- `start_point::an_open_boundary_refuses_a_pick_at_its_offset_cutter_start`\n\n`camcraft-app --test contour_dxf_sketch`:\n\n- `start_point::an_open_sketch_endpoint_pick_preserves_climb_and_chain_reverse`\n- `start_point::an_open_sketch_start_pick_requires_one_selected_chain`\n- `start_point::an_open_sketch_start_pick_follows_the_existing_wcs_yaw_mapping`\n\nPASS — twelve separate `cargo check --tests -p <package> -j 2` commands:\n`camcraft-kernel`, `camcraft-geometry`, `camcraft-cl`, `camcraft-tools`, `camcraft-sim`,\n`camcraft-motion`, `camcraft-post`, `camcraft-gcode`, `camcraft-gpu`, `camcraft-ui-kit`,\n`camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`. These include incoming product changes. Unchanged `xtask` is excluded.\n\nPASS — both strict scoped Clippy checks: motion in 25.7 seconds and app in 161.5 seconds:\n\n```text\ncargo clippy -j 2 -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings\ncargo clippy -j 2 -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings\n```\n\nPASS — the full unfiltered quick gate, 101/101 steps: two builds and 99 test steps, in 59.0 minutes:\n\n```text\ncargo xtask gate quick --base 2394b5ad1efc573b7b99a898a02cc4225b4d9893\n```\n\nThe run passed 2,858 tests, failed none and retained 102 existing ignored tests. Exit: 0.\nNo step failed, stalled or was skipped. The head and tree remained clean; goldens were unchanged.\nAll nine required example binaries passed: 80 tests, zero failed and four existing ignored tests.\n\n| Binary | Passed | Failed | Existing ignored |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `example_catalog` | 50 | 0 | 4 |\n| `example_catalog_adaptive` | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| `example_catalog_edge_work` | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| `first_part_programs` | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| `first_router_part` | 4 | 0 | 0 |\n| `first_4axis_part` | 4 | 0 | 0 |\n| `continuous_4axis_part` | 10 | 0 | 0 |\n| `tilt_basis_compat` | 7 | 0 | 0 |\n| `catalog_groove_part_off` | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n\nPASS — all eleven current required light twins across all three test steps, in 55.3 minutes:\n\n```text\ncargo xtask gate light --base 2394b5ad1efc573b7b99a898a02cc4225b4d9893 --only \"motion light:\" --only \"app light:\"\n```\n\n| Current light step | Passed | Failed | Ignored |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `motion light: lib` | 7 | 0 | 0 |\n| `motion light: adaptive2d` | 3 | 0 | 0 |\n| `app light: pocket_pass_start` | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe selection retains every current required twin and test step and omits only the broad prebuild.\nAll eleven executed twins passed, with zero failures or ignores. Exit: 0.\n\nNo physical machining, GUI runtime, UI snapshot, full heavy or release/cut result is claimed.\nThis P2 contribution requires no targeted heavy step.\n\n## Author refresh and final diff\n\nThe [independent contributor precheck](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/4505#issuecomment-7233341328)\nrequested an ordinary author refresh. The issue branch merged exact upstream `2394b5ad1efc573b7b99a898a02cc4225b4d9893`.\nThe open-boundary source guard remains before the avoid-aware dispatch.\nThe stock public source guard remains after the extracted helper's validation, side, offset and clearance checks.\nBoth requirements are preserved. These two hand resolutions are DELTA; an independent recheck must confirm both requirements.\nFork main was not changed by this author refresh.\n\nThe resulting diff against upstream contains only the twelve issue files: 335 insertions and seven deletions.\nThere is no process, version, manifest, lock, golden or snapshot delta. Upstream process version 166 is preserved.\nFork synced at v0.27.0. A final contributor precheck and a separate no-build readiness pass precede the ready flag.\n\nOwnership: [current writer record](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/1473#issuecomment-7233380150).\n\nProcess change: no\nEffort: max\nChangelog: 2D Contour accepts an exact natural start pick on one open DXF centerline and preserves the selected cut direction.\n\nRefs #1473",
